WEBVTT

01:31.590 --> 01:33.980
I have class now.

01:35.440 --> 01:37.360
Haven't I told you?

01:38.060 --> 01:39.990
Well, the time zone isn't my fault!

01:41.000 --> 01:42.460
That's perfect.

01:43.350 --> 01:45.540
Don't call me anymore.

01:49.400 --> 01:51.680
Good morning.

01:52.500 --> 01:53.610
Morning.

02:01.110 --> 02:03.360
<i>She's scary even on the phone.</i>

02:05.230 --> 02:08.310
This is technically your room, too.

02:08.310 --> 02:11.770
Don't mind me. Just come in, even 
if I'm in the middle of something.

02:13.780 --> 02:16.540
Th-Thank you.

02:16.540 --> 02:20.940
I hate the hesitant, weirdly 
polite way you talk.

02:21.760 --> 02:23.530
Are you mocking me?

02:23.930 --> 02:26.270
N-No, absolutely not.

02:26.270 --> 02:29.040
It reminds me of something. 
It pisses me off.

02:29.040 --> 02:30.230
Stop it.

02:30.230 --> 02:31.190
Yeah.

02:31.190 --> 02:32.330
Okay.

02:33.480 --> 02:36.750
<i>Her words are harsh, but I guess
 she's looking out for me.</i>

02:38.730 --> 02:39.550
What?

02:39.550 --> 02:42.850
Oh, you just remind me of someone I know.

02:42.850 --> 02:44.070
I see.

02:44.070 --> 02:47.030
I know someone a lot like you, too.

02:47.490 --> 02:51.750
Always timid, trying to read the room, 
benevolent in all the wrong ways...

02:52.290 --> 02:57.030
You seem to think things are okay 
as long as you put up with everything.

02:57.550 --> 02:58.820
I <i>hate</i> it!

02:59.820 --> 03:03.610
Don't go around saying people 
remind you of someone you know.

03:03.610 --> 03:04.370
Sorry.

03:05.650 --> 03:08.230
Why'd you come to the College, anyway?

03:08.810 --> 03:10.590
Planning on becoming a sorcerer?

03:10.830 --> 03:12.120
Nothing like that.

03:12.120 --> 03:14.560
It's not for a particularly 
important reason.

03:14.560 --> 03:17.130
It'd probably seem pretty silly to you.

03:17.640 --> 03:21.290
Do you think I'm so stupid I'd assume that 
when I haven't even asked what the reason is?

03:22.620 --> 03:24.840
I never said that.

03:25.410 --> 03:26.630
I'm done.

03:29.020 --> 03:30.600
Just finish getting ready.

03:31.250 --> 03:32.120
Right.

03:33.760 --> 03:34.920
Where's your lab coat?

03:36.120 --> 03:38.230
Our first class is pharmacology.

03:43.400 --> 03:45.510
I'm opening your closet.

03:47.740 --> 03:48.560
Here.

03:48.560 --> 03:50.760
Th-Thanks.

03:52.830 --> 03:54.310
That's all you needed to say.

04:01.140 --> 04:02.170
Okay.

04:06.040 --> 04:07.160
Um...

04:07.160 --> 04:08.060
Jasmine?

04:08.060 --> 04:09.140
Morning.

04:09.140 --> 04:10.470
Did you sleep in, too?

04:10.470 --> 04:11.680
Something like that.

04:12.690 --> 04:15.390
How can you stand sharing a room with her?

04:15.390 --> 04:17.370
She's abrasive, isn't she?

04:17.370 --> 04:19.050
Not really.

04:20.010 --> 04:23.690
I've never seen her getting 
along with anyone.

04:25.080 --> 04:28.910
Though, considering the Webster 
Tragedy, I can't blame her.

04:29.950 --> 04:31.900
The Webster Tragedy?

04:35.700 --> 04:38.580
Pretend you never heard that.

04:38.580 --> 04:39.690
Bye!

04:41.850 --> 04:43.370
You're gonna be late!

04:47.090 --> 04:49.960
Thanks for helping me clean up.

04:49.960 --> 04:51.680
I only taught you how to do it.

04:55.560 --> 04:57.600
So we have normal classes too, huh?

04:57.960 --> 05:02.900
It's not as though everyone who graduates 
is going to make a living as a sorcerer.

05:08.900 --> 05:11.870
Have you been any further than that?

05:09.770 --> 05:11.710
Isaac and Ivy.

05:15.250 --> 05:17.560
Well, I'm gonna go eat in my room.

05:17.560 --> 05:19.120
Huh? Sure...

05:22.300 --> 05:24.420
<i>I'm being avoided.</i>

05:24.950 --> 05:26.710
Hatori. Rian.

05:27.140 --> 05:28.830
You can call me Chise.

05:28.830 --> 05:31.270
In that case, call me Isaac, too.

05:31.270 --> 05:32.210
What about him?

05:32.510 --> 05:34.680
Zoe's a new student, too.

05:35.210 --> 05:37.020
I've been teaching him stuff.

05:37.530 --> 05:41.660
I mean, I'm not from the prestigious 
Seven Shields or anything.

05:42.010 --> 05:46.710
But that also means I know how to teach 
in a way that makes sense to people.

05:47.520 --> 05:49.010
Prestigious?

05:49.360 --> 05:50.850
The Seven Shields?

05:52.490 --> 05:59.790
The Seven Shields are the seven distinguished
 families that founded the College.

06:01.040 --> 06:03.280
Roseingrave the Employer,

06:03.280 --> 06:05.440
St. George the Hunter,

06:05.440 --> 06:07.630
Rickenbacker the Doctor,

06:07.630 --> 06:09.450
Forsyth the Strategist,

06:09.450 --> 06:11.570
Hohenheim the Alchemist,

06:11.570 --> 06:13.630
Nightingale the Musician,

06:13.630 --> 06:15.310
Scrimgeour the Protector.

06:15.880 --> 06:20.000
You know how a lot of mages 
and sorcerers died in the war?

06:20.000 --> 06:25.310
The Seven were concerned that sorcery would 
die away, so they quietly built this College.

06:25.570 --> 06:29.320
To be honest, you don't want to 
get too involved with any of them.

06:29.320 --> 06:30.600
What do you mean by that?

06:30.600 --> 06:32.120
You're different, Rian.

06:32.730 --> 06:36.250
Specifically, the Scrimgeour 
family produced a lot

06:36.250 --> 06:38.870
of gifted sorcerers who 
would serve as protectors.

06:39.340 --> 06:44.340
There's still a lot of fighting, so 
sorcerers ask them for their protection.

06:44.580 --> 06:46.830
They're like bodyguards.

06:46.830 --> 06:48.000
I see.

06:49.840 --> 06:53.170
Well, I'm leaving home, so 
it's not my problem anymore.

06:55.840 --> 06:56.560
Oh...

06:57.290 --> 07:00.990
Do you know what the
 "Webster Tragedy" is about?

07:00.990 --> 07:02.790
Webster?

07:02.790 --> 07:03.980
You mean Lucy?

07:04.330 --> 07:05.490
Chise.

07:05.490 --> 07:07.700
Who did you hear about that from?

07:08.900 --> 07:10.940
From Jasmine. The twin.

07:13.150 --> 07:17.810
Looks like this is one of those things that 
we little people are better off not knowing.

07:17.810 --> 07:19.670
Seems that way.

07:20.620 --> 07:21.490
Crap!

07:21.990 --> 07:23.980
The next class is about to start.

07:23.980 --> 07:25.180
I'll see you there.

07:25.180 --> 07:26.920
Wait up!

07:44.730 --> 07:46.260
We run into each other a lot.

07:46.900 --> 07:49.030
We're roommates. Of course we do.

07:49.290 --> 07:50.730
Oh... yeah.

07:56.950 --> 07:58.110
Ivy.

07:58.820 --> 08:01.620
Have I done something to you?

08:02.980 --> 08:04.670
If I have...

08:18.140 --> 08:19.540
Give those back!

08:19.540 --> 08:21.750
Looks like you didn't hear her.

08:21.750 --> 08:23.080
Just give them back!

08:23.080 --> 08:24.020
I need those!

08:24.020 --> 08:26.730
Look, I don't care if you 
hate her or whatever.

08:26.730 --> 08:29.940
But it pisses me off when
 people ignore others.

08:29.940 --> 08:33.090
You don't know who she is!

08:33.090 --> 08:34.060
What?

08:34.060 --> 08:34.850
Hatori!

08:35.410 --> 08:37.270
You know better than anyone!

08:37.740 --> 08:40.270
You probably think you've 
managed to disguise yourself.

08:40.820 --> 08:42.530
But I can tell.

08:43.740 --> 08:46.030
You're a monster!

08:49.930 --> 08:52.570
So what's that Tragedy about?

08:52.570 --> 08:54.250
You're better off not knowing.

08:54.250 --> 08:55.370
You said it yourself.

09:04.340 --> 09:05.370
Snakes?

09:10.820 --> 09:12.400
Listen up, Zoe.

09:12.400 --> 09:14.390
You're special.

09:15.510 --> 09:16.970
<i>Special...</i>

09:20.350 --> 09:22.280
His hair turned into snakes.

09:22.280 --> 09:23.820
Don't tell me...

09:24.590 --> 09:25.600
Don't look at me!

09:28.080 --> 09:29.780
Wait, who was that?

09:30.200 --> 09:31.480
Ivy...

09:31.480 --> 09:32.250
Zoe?

09:32.250 --> 09:34.730
Ruth, please.

09:34.730 --> 09:35.370
Got it.

09:35.810 --> 09:36.590
A familiar?!

09:37.050 --> 09:38.420
What happened?

09:38.420 --> 09:40.980
His headphones got taken off.

09:40.980 --> 09:42.220
Then he got angry, and...

09:42.700 --> 09:44.550
Those aren't headphones.

09:44.890 --> 09:46.020
They're earmuffs.

09:46.020 --> 09:47.480
To keep sound out.

09:47.480 --> 09:50.210
People with hypersensitive 
hearing wear them.

09:50.930 --> 09:53.800
Hearing too much is a problem
 for them, apparently.

09:53.800 --> 09:56.430
They can't filter out auditory 
information by themselves.

09:58.800 --> 09:59.730
Where to?

10:00.100 --> 10:01.690
I have to apologize.

10:02.460 --> 10:04.580
We're going to have to deal with this.

10:04.580 --> 10:05.780
Yeah.

10:08.020 --> 10:08.900
Aren't you coming?

10:09.300 --> 10:11.410
You're sure being kind, nobleman.

10:11.980 --> 10:13.100
My family is irrelevant—

10:13.100 --> 10:14.290
They <i>are</i> relevant.

10:15.630 --> 10:18.800
Webster, as long as you're 
the one holding those,

10:18.800 --> 10:21.560
don't you also owe an apology?

10:32.500 --> 10:35.150
So he's a Gorgon.

10:35.430 --> 10:36.570
A Gorgon?

10:36.840 --> 10:39.160
A monster that comes up in Greek mythology.

10:39.810 --> 10:45.500
"Gorgon" was originally the name of an old 
god, but it's used as a family name now.

10:46.790 --> 10:51.380
They get treated the same as 
anyone else now, but in the past,

10:51.380 --> 10:53.980
they were hunted for their 
flesh, bodily fluids, and eyes.

10:54.700 --> 10:56.570
Their kind need to be protected.

10:57.640 --> 11:00.960
I can't believe one of them would 
be in the College, though.

11:00.960 --> 11:02.030
Why's that?

11:02.030 --> 11:04.430
Gorgons can't speak with humans.

11:04.430 --> 11:07.670
Their vocal range is quite a bit
 different from a human's.

11:08.230 --> 11:12.090
And worst of all, their eyes...

11:12.090 --> 11:14.930
They immobilize anyone they make eye contact with.

11:15.920 --> 11:17.740
Supposedly, anyway.

11:19.190 --> 11:21.370
Where are we even going?

11:22.790 --> 11:25.080
That won't be a problem.

11:34.210 --> 11:35.380
Where are we?

11:36.410 --> 11:37.890
The private gardens.

11:38.470 --> 11:41.620
They're set up so that you 
don't know who's inside.

11:41.620 --> 11:43.720
It suppresses sound to some extent, too.

11:46.760 --> 11:49.610
The smell of greenery is oddly strong here.

11:49.610 --> 11:51.060
It's making him hard to track.

11:51.520 --> 11:52.380
All right.

11:54.000 --> 11:55.530
Now I can follow him.

11:55.530 --> 11:56.390
Yeah.

12:16.810 --> 12:18.090
Ivy?

12:20.110 --> 12:21.590
Why?

12:21.890 --> 12:25.040
Are you here to laugh at me?
 Because I'm a failure?

12:25.040 --> 12:26.450
Damn it...

12:26.450 --> 12:28.580
I was doing all right until now.

12:28.580 --> 12:29.510
Shit!

12:29.790 --> 12:32.470
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

12:35.280 --> 12:36.560
I told you to stay away!

12:40.840 --> 12:41.810
Sorry.

12:42.120 --> 12:45.500
I know you're not trying to hurt me.

12:45.500 --> 12:46.550
Huh?

12:47.080 --> 12:49.320
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

12:51.530 --> 12:52.880
Take them back.

12:53.320 --> 12:55.690
Sorry for taking them from you.

12:56.450 --> 12:58.140
Y-Yeah...

13:03.790 --> 13:06.270
I heard it's for soundproofing. 
You can hear me, though, yeah?

13:06.270 --> 13:07.170
You good now?

13:07.170 --> 13:07.950
Feeling all right?

13:07.950 --> 13:08.720
How about you, Chise?

13:08.720 --> 13:09.650
Did you get bit?

13:09.650 --> 13:10.940
Are you okay with snakes?

13:10.940 --> 13:12.900
I-I'm fine.

13:13.290 --> 13:14.300
Look at that.

13:14.300 --> 13:16.080
She can do fine when she tries.

13:16.080 --> 13:18.780
My older sister's like that, too.

13:19.090 --> 13:22.070
Ivy, are you a Gorgon?

13:22.070 --> 13:23.830
Why are you at the College?

13:24.980 --> 13:27.680
Oh, I'm not accusing you of anything.

13:27.680 --> 13:30.040
I just want to know why.

13:30.040 --> 13:31.660
You don't have to answer if you don't want to.

13:31.660 --> 13:33.930
Everyone's got something they 
don't want to talk about.

13:34.580 --> 13:36.340
Will you keep it a secret?

13:36.340 --> 13:38.620
We can form a contract if you need.

13:39.000 --> 13:41.480
Must you do absolutely
 <i>everything</i> by the book?

13:41.480 --> 13:43.660
Contracts are important.

13:43.930 --> 13:45.600
No, it's fine.

13:46.210 --> 13:48.600
It's honestly been a bit annoying.

13:49.530 --> 13:51.510
I'm better off being found out.

13:52.580 --> 13:55.450
This was my first time coming 
to a place like this.

14:02.810 --> 14:08.210
My mom was born in a secret Gorgon 
settlement by the Black Sea.

14:08.660 --> 14:13.290
And she met my dad, who was a sorcerer
and demi-human languages researcher.

14:14.450 --> 14:18.060
They laid an egg. That was me.

14:18.060 --> 14:18.950
An egg?!

14:18.950 --> 14:20.430
What?!

14:20.430 --> 14:22.600
Is there a problem with me 
being hatched from an egg?!

14:22.600 --> 14:27.540
I mean, I guess eggs are more 
productive—I mean, more stable.

14:27.820 --> 14:33.080
I've always been going back and 
forth between snake and human.

14:33.080 --> 14:35.670
I've always needed to have 
earmuffs and goggles with me.

14:36.980 --> 14:41.780
I'm unusually affected by light and 
unusually sensitive to smells.

14:42.400 --> 14:44.940
And I have almost no ability to use my eyes.

14:45.750 --> 14:50.770
Without my special earmuffs,
my hair tries to turn into snakes.

14:50.770 --> 14:52.200
My body sucks.

14:52.620 --> 14:54.080
That must have been tough.

14:54.500 --> 14:56.750
So why did you come to the College?

14:57.250 --> 14:58.840
My dad...

15:00.220 --> 15:02.260
I'm afraid of going outside.

15:02.640 --> 15:05.300
People tell me there's something 
wrong with me even in the village.

15:06.010 --> 15:08.960
I'm afraid humans are going 
to tell me I'm weird, too.

15:09.260 --> 15:11.640
Everyone's got secrets.

15:11.640 --> 15:13.980
Despite that, people are generally nice.

15:13.980 --> 15:15.980
I'm sure you'll make friends, too.

15:15.980 --> 15:19.920
So go to the College and get some studying done.

15:19.920 --> 15:22.720
I'm so worried about you, 
I can't even go do my fieldwork.

15:23.350 --> 15:25.640
He was just thinking about his fieldwork!

15:25.640 --> 15:26.990
He's a sorcerer.

15:26.990 --> 15:28.730
He's a researcher, after all.

15:28.730 --> 15:30.870
Are sorcerers all like this?

15:32.220 --> 15:36.200
So that's why I'm here.
 To train myself to be outside.

15:36.730 --> 15:38.650
What about you, Hatori?

15:38.650 --> 15:40.590
You aren't human either, are you?

15:40.590 --> 15:42.040
Well...

15:42.480 --> 15:44.240
It might be because of this.

15:44.240 --> 15:46.400
Wow, it's pitch black.

15:46.400 --> 15:48.140
What have you done?

15:48.500 --> 15:51.960
Well, I was cursed by a dragon recently.

15:51.960 --> 15:53.090
A dragon?!

15:53.420 --> 15:55.750
Is this what dragons smell like?

15:55.750 --> 15:57.930
It smells so toxic.

15:57.930 --> 16:00.180
I think that's because it's a curse.

16:00.790 --> 16:04.860
As Gorgons, we're taught that 
our ancestors were dragons.

16:04.860 --> 16:08.130
That's why we get riled up
 when we see dragons.

16:08.440 --> 16:10.540
I wonder if that's why I get annoyed.

16:11.280 --> 16:13.280
I do feel bad about what I did.

16:13.280 --> 16:17.510
But here I am, trying really hard to keep 
myself from sticking my tongues out,

16:17.510 --> 16:19.540
when this person comes along like catnip...

16:20.080 --> 16:22.190
You get what I'm going through, right?

16:22.660 --> 16:24.080
Y-Yeah.

16:25.790 --> 16:28.790
Hatori, is there something 
other than the dragon...

16:28.790 --> 16:30.200
S-Sorry!

16:30.200 --> 16:31.580
My snakes!

16:32.270 --> 16:33.580
It's fine.

16:34.300 --> 16:37.160
They're such a nice spring green.
 I'd love a dye in this color.

16:37.820 --> 16:39.070
It's beautiful.

16:41.060 --> 16:42.670
<i>It'll be fine, Zoe.</i>

16:43.540 --> 16:46.600
You're special, for better or worse.

16:46.910 --> 16:49.240
We were the ones who birthed you that way,

16:49.240 --> 16:51.440
but we don't regret it, 
so we can't apologize for it.

16:51.880 --> 16:55.160
So at least we'll create
 an opportunity for you

16:55.160 --> 16:57.900
to meet someone who would 
say you're beautiful.

16:59.040 --> 17:02.750
<i>I hate to admit it, but he got 
his wish sooner than I expected.</i>

17:02.750 --> 17:04.940
Besides, would anyone here 
really be surprised

17:04.930 --> 17:07.100
to see someone with snakes for a hair?

17:07.100 --> 17:09.160
Look at the instructors.

17:09.160 --> 17:11.720
The instructors are all human.

17:12.440 --> 17:15.210
I'm scared, though. Really.

17:15.860 --> 17:20.210
There are still people who fall victim 
to hunters and never come home.

17:20.730 --> 17:24.330
So you're not here to
 become a sorcerer, then?

17:24.330 --> 17:25.950
Of course not.

17:25.950 --> 17:28.120
That's a human thing to do, isn't it?

17:29.430 --> 17:31.100
By the way, what do you want to do?

17:31.100 --> 17:34.570
If you want to keep it secret, we should 
consider using a contract spell—

17:39.920 --> 17:42.080
I caught her listening.

17:45.280 --> 17:46.530
Philomela.

17:47.640 --> 17:52.350
She followed us and tried 
to eavesdrop or peep.

17:52.350 --> 17:54.010
What do you think you're doing?

17:54.490 --> 17:56.890
Practicing...

17:57.180 --> 18:00.340
Her family specializes in intelligence.

18:00.760 --> 18:04.720
Are they making you do
 that even in the College?

18:07.030 --> 18:11.200
I've told you to stop going silent every 
time you're in trouble, haven't I?

18:11.610 --> 18:13.820
What's your relationship with her?

18:13.820 --> 18:15.060
She's my second cousin.

18:16.510 --> 18:18.730
Did you hear what we were saying in there?

18:19.340 --> 18:21.740
About Chise and Ivy.

18:22.070 --> 18:24.730
You got past the noise suppression sorcery.

18:25.220 --> 18:27.030
Are you going to sell me to someone?

18:27.660 --> 18:31.550
I have no intention of telling anyone.

18:31.870 --> 18:33.590
And if someone asks you?

18:33.920 --> 18:35.270
I don't know.

18:35.270 --> 18:38.600
I don't have the right to refuse.

18:40.270 --> 18:41.710
We have no choice.

18:41.710 --> 18:43.370
We'll use the contract spell.

18:44.610 --> 18:48.010
It'll burn your throat if 
you try to tell someone.

18:48.010 --> 18:50.620
And it'll burn your fingers 
if you try to write it down.

18:50.620 --> 18:52.510
That's a bit much...

18:53.010 --> 18:57.570
Um, so... in my case, I'm just trying to 
keep my secret as much as I can.

18:57.570 --> 19:00.630
But I'd really rather you 
not tell anyone about Ivy.

19:01.420 --> 19:04.490
If that's an order,
I'd prefer you make it clear.

19:05.520 --> 19:06.780
It's not an order.

19:07.610 --> 19:08.660
Um...

19:10.120 --> 19:12.800
It's a request, I guess.

19:16.960 --> 19:18.180
All right.

19:20.830 --> 19:22.950
Blessings upon they who adhere.

19:23.360 --> 19:26.050
Punishment upon they who breach.

19:27.320 --> 19:29.570
A warning to they who possess wisdom.

19:30.170 --> 19:32.770
A song of doom to 
the mouths of the ignorant.

19:33.890 --> 19:36.060
A silver tongue bares wisdom.

19:36.350 --> 19:39.080
A lead tongue is forsaken by the Lord.

19:39.670 --> 19:41.970
Thou shalt not speak.

19:42.400 --> 19:44.580
Thou shalt not write.

19:45.270 --> 19:48.770
The ring of the pact, 
the snake in a river of grief.

19:49.840 --> 19:52.080
Consume the flesh of they who speak.

19:52.860 --> 19:55.100
Drink the blood of they who write.

19:55.860 --> 20:00.270
The song of betrayal
 will not be forgiven.

20:08.380 --> 20:09.900
And the pact is made.

20:16.410 --> 20:17.430
Chise...

20:18.330 --> 20:20.780
I haven't apologized yet.

20:20.780 --> 20:23.490
Sorry for ignoring you and 
getting angry and stuff.

20:25.060 --> 20:26.670
I wasn't bothered by it.

20:33.170 --> 20:36.070
I still don't trust you.

20:36.540 --> 20:38.520
Sneaking around like that...

20:38.970 --> 20:43.430
My family died because of people like you.

20:56.940 --> 20:59.730
I heard you told Chise about the Websters.

20:59.730 --> 21:01.100
Jasmine.

21:03.620 --> 21:05.660
You shouldn't bring that family up.

21:06.110 --> 21:08.490
It just slipped out by accident.

21:08.880 --> 21:11.750
Bear in mind that you're a member
 of one of the Seven Shields families.

21:12.770 --> 21:16.570
You Scrimgeours sure are wise.

21:16.570 --> 21:19.130
Spare me the self-depreciation, St. George.

21:19.500 --> 21:24.470
Besides, I've already decided 
I'm going to be by myself.

21:24.830 --> 21:28.430
Do you honestly think we 
can abandon our own blood?

21:33.010 --> 21:34.100
Rian!

21:37.400 --> 21:38.450
What's his problem?

21:38.450 --> 21:39.960
He's so aggressive.

21:45.160 --> 21:47.540
You were here, Violet?

21:47.540 --> 21:51.210
Rian is too condescending.

21:51.570 --> 21:54.230
He puts on that face like 
he's above everyone else.

21:55.080 --> 21:56.620
Truly arrogant.

21:58.820 --> 22:02.220
If things get really bad, we can 
find a master and run away.

22:02.220 --> 22:02.890
Huh?

22:03.200 --> 22:09.090
Mister Ainsworth said we might have 
aptitude to become mages, remember?

22:09.740 --> 22:11.090
But...

22:14.640 --> 22:19.030
We can make all the escape routes we need.

22:19.410 --> 22:20.550
Why not?
